PLIC spec semantics + 3-bit WARL priorities (branch plic-spec, #21, 2026-10-16)
===============================================================================

Base: fork main 3feef0c (#22 plic_tb + #18). Changes in rtl/soc/muserisc_plic.sv,
the soc_tb C++ PLIC model and plic_tb's reference model:
- claim: highest-priority pending enabled source with priority > 0,
  independent of the threshold (threshold gates only EIP);
- completion for a source not enabled for the context: ignored;
- priority/threshold registers WARL with 3 implemented bits.

== plic_tb (proves the fix) ==
New directed checks: claim of a source whose priority is <= threshold
(returns it, EIP stays low), completion from a context the source is not
enabled for (ignored, pending stays clear), WARL readback (0xffffffff -> 7,
byte merge 0xfd -> 5, threshold 0x12345678 -> 0). The previous RTL
(main) fails this plic_tb: 81,758 of 200,133 checks in a 100k-cycle run.
plic_tb seed 0x91c (core-test)   PLIC TB PASS (4,000,133 checks, 2M cycles, 93,552 claim reads)
plic_tb seed 0x5eed, 4M cycles   PLIC TB PASS (8,000,133 checks)

